# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a managed workflow job with `job.cancel()`, the workflow also tries to cancel the QPU work that the workflow started:\n"
msgstr "Când anulezi un job de workflow gestionat cu `job.cancel()`, workflow-ul încearcă să anuleze și munca QPU pe care a pornit-o:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions and batches.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's sessions and batches, which also cancels their queued jobs.\n"
msgstr "**Sesiuni și batch-uri.** Workflow-ul anulează fiecare sesiune și fiecare batch al workflow-ului, ceea ce anulează și joburile lor din coadă.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other primitive jobs.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's other primitive jobs that are still queued or running.\n"
msgstr "**Alte joburi primitive.** Workflow-ul anulează fiecare dintre celelalte joburi primitive ale workflow-ului care sunt încă în coadă sau rulează.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message for each QPU job and session, so you can check what was canceled:\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` returnează un mesaj pentru fiecare job QPU și sesiune, astfel încât poți verifica ce a fost anulat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a workflow that ran in a batch, the message looks like the following:\n"
msgstr "Pentru un workflow care a rulat într-un batch, mesajul arată astfel:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the client cannot create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, it cancels only the managed workflow job. Cancel the QPU jobs yourself with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Dacă clientul nu poate crea un `QiskitRuntimeService` din credențialele tale locale, anulează doar jobul de workflow gestionat. Anulează tu joburile QPU cu ID-urile lor din `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a workflow stops a job itself, for example because it reached the 24-hour limit, it does not cancel its QPU jobs. Cancel them with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Când un workflow oprește el însuși un job, de exemplu pentru că a atins limita de 24 de ore, nu își anulează joburile QPU. Anulează-le cu ID-urile lor din `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the scheduler's timeout and blocked-account stops (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout, FleetsJobCanceller) cancel only the fleet. Only the user stop endpoint (StopJobUseCase) cancels runtime jobs. Confirm whether this is intended before publishing. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot QPU jobs in a workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Depanează joburile QPU dintr-un workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` raises `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | The code runs in your local notebook, not in a managed workflow job. Use `QiskitRuntimeService()` locally. |\n"
"| `update_status()` returns `False`, and the logs show `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | The value is not one of the `Job` constants, or the job is no longer active. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` returns `[]`. | The workflow created its service with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, or it has not run a primitive yet. |\n"
"| A session's jobs are not tracked. | The session was created from a backend of a different service. Get the backend from `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| The workflow logs show `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | The workflow could not record a primitive job. The primitive job still runs, but it is not tracked. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` shows `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | The client could not create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, so it canceled only the managed workflow job. |\n"
"| `client.job()` fails with `Job [...] not found`. | The job ID is wrong, or the job belongs to another user. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problemă | Cauză |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` ridică `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | Codul rulează în notebookul tău local, nu într-un job de workflow gestionat. Folosește `QiskitRuntimeService()` local. |\n"
"| `update_status()` returnează `False`, iar logurile arată `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | Valoarea nu este una dintre constantele `Job` sau jobul nu mai este activ. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` returnează `[]`. | Workflow-ul și-a creat serviciul cu `QiskitRuntimeService()` sau nu a rulat încă nicio primitivă. |\n"
"| Joburile unei sesiuni nu sunt urmărite. | Sesiunea a fost creată dintr-un backend al unui alt serviciu. Obține backend-ul din `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| Logurile workflow-ului arată `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | Workflow-ul nu a putut înregistra un job primitiv. Jobul primitiv rulează în continuare, dar nu este urmărit. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` arată `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | Clientul nu a putut crea un `QiskitRuntimeService` din credențialele tale locale, deci a anulat doar jobul de workflow gestionat. |\n"
"| `client.job()` eșuează cu `Job [...] not found`. | ID-ul jobului este greșit sau jobul aparține altui utilizator. |\n"

